course: dictionary
lesson: 2867
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «Dominion» is one of these words. Its main meaning is power or control over people, land or things, as in «have dominion over».
explain: The sentence «In 1867 several colonies joined to form the Dominion of Canada, which is celebrated every year on Canada Day, 1 July.» uses dominion as a name. The clues are that colonies joined to form it and that it is celebrated, so here it means a self-governing country, not power or control.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Several colonies joined to form a self-governing country» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning. Always ask which meaning fits the clues around the word.
fact: Dominion is a noun: one dominion, two dominions.
fact: «Dominion» means power or control over people, land or things.
fact: «Dominion» can also mean a land or territory ruled by a king or government.
fact: In history, «Dominion» was the name for some self-governing countries of the British Empire, such as Canada, Australia and New Zealand.
fact: Useful phrases are «have dominion over», «under the dominion of» and «Dominion Day».
exercise: «In 1867 several colonies joined to form the Dominion of Canada.» What does dominion mean in this sentence? | A small hill | *A self-governing country | A sweet pudding | A type of bird
exercise: Which phrase uses dominion to mean power or control? | celebrated every year | *have dominion over | several colonies | Canada Day
exercise: Find and copy the word from «In 1867 several colonies joined to form the Dominion of Canada» that tells you when it was formed. | *1867 | several | Canada | colonies
test: In the Bible, God gives people dominion over the animals. What do many Christians understand this to mean? | A right to hunt without limits | A holiday from work | *A duty to care for creation | Power to ignore the animals
test: Which word is linked to dominion, meaning looking after the earth? | blossom | ferocity | sunshine | *stewardship
exam: Which meaning fits «The king had dominion over the lands north of the river.»? | A type of tree | A loud noise | *Power and control over land | A small meal
